# r371-r374 health-check SKILL.md
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-M-0035 P:RULE-M-0455 | R: liveness/readiness distinct, readiness may depend on required capabilities; P: include only dependencies required for meaningful readiness.
RD EXAMPLE_GENERAL R:RULE-M-0034 P:RULE-M-0456 | R: health checks cheap, no expensive or mutating database work; P: database health is a lightweight connectivity check.
SPLIT X:BF-M-0079 | a@81-84: Check an external dependency only when it matters to readiness and avoid readiness cascades; prefer a lightweight check of the needed capability. | b@95-97: Keep probe responses small and protect detailed diagnostics with network or authorization controls. | c@113-115: Avoid Error-level logs for every normal failed probe.
SD P:RULE-M-0457 X:BF-M-0079#a | S: readiness checks M: P AVOID, X no modality E: none in either T: none | P's 'remote dependency chains' wording (lines 127-128) restates the same cascade concern
SD P:RULE-M-0458 X:BF-M-0079#b | S: health probe responses M: P MUST, X no modality E: none in either T: none
SD P:EXTRA-M-0144 X:BF-M-0079#c | S: health probe logging M: P AVOID, X no modality E: none in either T: none
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-M-0036 P:RULE-M-0458 | R: public health responses never expose secrets or internal diagnostics; P: small responses, detailed diagnostics protected.
RD BROADER_NARROWER R:RULE-M-0035 P:RULE-M-0459 | R/rule includes 'readiness stays unhealthy until required startup work completes'; P (skill) states only that clause.
RD DIFFERENT_STRENGTH R:RULE-M-0034 P:RULE-M-0460 | R/rule: health checks stay cheap (MUST); P (skill): avoid expensive queries, long timeouts, large allocations, workflows (AVOID).
