RD EXAMPLE_GENERAL R:RULE-M-0025#a P:RULE-M-0476 | P: 204 for successful operations without a response body.
SPLIT X:BF-M-0081 | a@78-81: Choose consistently whether a repeated DELETE of an absent resource returns 204 or 404, and do not mix them between equivalent resources. | b@87-89: Use 304 only for conditional requests whose cached representation is still valid, never as a generic business 'nothing changed' response. | c@95-99: 400 is for an invalid HTTP request (malformed, binding failure, uninterpretable), not for authentication failure.
